          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Using Theorem 6.2, prove that the line joining the mid-points of any two sides of a triangle is parallel to the third side. (Recall that you have done it in Class IX)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.389,
            0.593,
            0.471
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ABCD is a trapezium in which AB || DC and its diagonals intersect each other at the point O. Show that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\frac { \\mathrm { A O } } { \\mathrm { B O } } } = { \\frac { \\mathrm { C O } } { \\mathrm { D O } } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.612,
            0.305,
            0.881,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": [
