              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 6.21"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.479,
            0.9,
            0.543
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The diagonals of a quadrilateral ABCD intersect each other at the point O such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\frac { \\mathrm { A O } } { \\mathrm { B O } } } = { \\frac { \\mathrm { C O } } { \\mathrm { D O } } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Show that ABCD is a trapezium."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.566,
            0.514,
            0.586
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6.4 Criteria for Similarity of Triangles"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.593,
            0.9,
            0.632
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the previous section, we stated that two triangles are similar, if (i) their corresponding angles are equal and (ii) their corresponding sides are in the same ratio (or proportion)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.637,
            0.463,
            0.655
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "That is, in "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta   \\mathrm { A B C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and   DEF, if"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.662,
            0.559,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A} = \\angle \\mathrm{D}, \\angle \\mathrm{B} = \\angle \\mathrm{E}, \\angle \\mathrm{C} = \\angle \\mathrm{F}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.695,
            0.825,
            0.735
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{\\mathrm{AB}}{\\mathrm{DE}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{BC}}{\\mathrm{EE}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{CA}}{\\mathrm{FD}}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " then the two triangles are similar (see Fig. 6.22)."
            }
          ]
        },
